  "$status": "Asking who on the list is here right now, and asking what is on the list at all. The two commands swap letters between the two questions, which is the sort of thing that makes a fallback look like it works until you read the replies.",
  "status": [
    {
      "kind": "MONITOR",
      "here": "MONITOR S",
      "list": "MONITOR L"
    },
    {
      "kind": "WATCH",
      "here": "WATCH L",
      "list": "WATCH S"
    }
  ],
  "$roster": "Every watched nick on every network as one list. Friends used to be a section under whichever network you were looking at, so a person watched on a network you had not opened today was simply not on screen. Online first because the list answers \"is anyone around?\", then by name, then by network — and never merged, because rowan on one network is not rowan on another.",
  "roster": [
    {
      "name": "online first, then by name",
      "watched": [
        {
          "serverId": "s1",
          "network": "netslum",
          "nick": "sam",
          "online": false
        },
        {
          "serverId": "s2",
          "network": "libera",
          "nick": "rowan",
          "online": true
        },
        {
          "serverId": "s1",
          "network": "netslum",
          "nick": "jo",
          "online": true
        }
      ],
      "labels": [
        "jo@netslum",
        "rowan@libera",
        "sam@netslum"
      ]
    },
    {
